// SOURCE OF TRUTH — this is the copy `firebase deploy` reads, because only this
// project has a `.firebaserc`. `app_v2/storage.rules` is a mirror: edit this
// file first and keep the two bodies byte-identical below their headers.
//
// Firebase Storage is RETIRED in this project. This file is the honest record of
// that state, not an upload surface:
//   • Proposal photos and meal photos go to Cloudinary (Unsigned Direct Upload);
//     no code path in the mobile app or the admin panel writes here.
//   • The `firebase_storage` package is in NEITHER app's pubspec, and neither
//     `lib/` tree mentions `FirebaseStorage` — so nothing in shipped code can
//     even reach this bucket.
//
// Every write is therefore closed unconditionally. One piece of history is
// worth keeping: the rules deployed before this rewrite granted
// `allow write: if request.auth != null` on /meal_images, and because the
// mobile app signs in anonymously the moment a meal is proposed, that rule let
// any device on any network write unlimited, arbitrary-type objects into the
// bucket.
//
// Reads stay open on exactly the two legacy prefixes below, and deliberately:
// rows seeded before the Cloudinary move still carry /meal_images/... or
// /staging_meal_images/<uid>/... URLs in their `imageUrl` field, and closing
// those reads would not protect anything — it would only blank the photos of
// existing data. Newly written rows never reference Storage.
//
// `/staging_meal_images/{uid}/{fileName}` is NOT dead code even though nothing
// uploads to it any more: this dashboard still renders the stored `imageUrl` of
// pending proposals (admin_dashboard_screen.dart, staging triage list and
// dialog), and pending documents created before the Cloudinary move point at
// this path. Delete this block only once those legacy rows are purged or their
// URLs rewritten to Cloudinary — until then it is a read-only tombstone.
rules_version = '2';
service firebase.storage {
  match /b/{bucket}/o {
    // Legacy, read-only: meal photos seeded before the Cloudinary move.
    match /meal_images/{fileName} {
      allow read: if true;
      allow write: if false;
    }
    // Legacy, read-only: staging ("proposal") photos seeded before the
    // Cloudinary move — still displayed by this dashboard. See header.
    match /staging_meal_images/{uid}/{fileName} {
      allow read: if true;
      allow write: if false;
    }
    // Anything else in the bucket is unreachable in both directions.
    match /{allPaths=**} {
      allow read, write: if false;
    }
  }
}
